        "subject": "LU-20918 rpm: install modules under /usr/lib on SLES 16",
        "message": "LU-20918 rpm: install modules under /usr/lib on SLES 16\n\nSLES 16 is usr-merged, and weak-modules2 only searches\n/usr/lib/modules for kernel modules. Modules installed under\n/lib/modules are not seen by it, so they are not handled when the\nkernel package is updated.\n\nFor suse_version >= 1600, make lustre.spec.in use /usr/lib/modules:\n\n- set modules_fs_path to /usr/lib/modules/%{_kver}/%{kmoddir}\n- after \"make install\", move $RPM_BUILD_ROOT/lib/modules to\n  $RPM_BUILD_ROOT/usr/lib/modules and remove the empty lib directory\n- run the find-debuginfo.sh chmod step on /usr/lib/modules\n\nOther distributions continue to use /lib/modules.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manhong Dai <manhong.dai@netapp.com>\nChange-Id: I0aab3112e83cb5d8d47dd953c912bd337fdac1a8\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
